From: Chokri Hammedi <52697989+blue0x1@users.noreply.github.com>
Subject: [PATCH] graphics: no conditional rendering on the PS4's GPUs

RADV lists VK_EXT_conditional_rendering on the PS4's GPUs (Liverpool and
Gladius), but their command processor never finishes the SET_PREDICATION
packet: the gfx ring times out, the GPU reset fails ("asic atom init
failed") and the screen stays off until the PS4 restarts. KytyPS5 sends that
packet the first time it clears a color target from its metadata on the GPU,
which Hollow Knight: Silksong (PPSA12544) does while it starts.

On these GPUs (AMD 0x9920 to 0x9924) the feature is now left off, so the
color metadata is read back instead, as on a GPU without the extension.
KYTY_CONDITIONAL_RENDERING=1 turns it on anyway, and =0 turns it off on any
GPU.

Found with RADV_DEBUG=hang on a PS4 Pro: the last trace point reached is the
one before the first SET_PREDICATION. With this patch Silksong reaches its
title screen there.
---
diff --git a/src/graphics/presentation/window/vulkanWindow.cpp b/src/graphics/presentation/window/vulkanWindow.cpp
index 637385e..211f628 100644
--- a/src/graphics/presentation/window/vulkanWindow.cpp
+++ b/src/graphics/presentation/window/vulkanWindow.cpp
@@ -25,6 +25,7 @@
 #include <algorithm>
 #include <cmath>
 #include <cstdio>
+#include <cstdlib>
 #include <cstring>
 #include <fmt/format.h>
 #include <memory>
@@ -507,7 +508,22 @@ static vk::Device VulkanCreateDevice(GraphicContext&          graphics,
 		graphics.device_clock_period_ps = static_cast<uint32_t>(
 		    std::lround(graphics.physical_device_properties.limits.timestampPeriod * 1000.0f));
 	}
-	graphics.conditional_rendering_enabled = conditional_rendering.conditionalRendering;
+	// The PS4's GPUs (Liverpool 0x9920-0x9923, Gladius 0x9924) list conditional rendering,
+	// but their command processor never finishes SET_PREDICATION: the GPU hangs and cannot
+	// be reset. Color metadata is read back on them instead. KYTY_CONDITIONAL_RENDERING=1
+	// (or 0, on any GPU) overrides this.
+	bool conditional_rendering_usable = !(graphics.physical_device_properties.vendorID == 0x1002u &&
+	                                      graphics.physical_device_properties.deviceID >= 0x9920u &&
+	                                      graphics.physical_device_properties.deviceID <= 0x9924u);
+	if (const char* force = std::getenv("KYTY_CONDITIONAL_RENDERING");
+	    force != nullptr && *force != 0) {
+		conditional_rendering_usable = *force != '0';
+	}
+	if (conditional_rendering.conditionalRendering && !conditional_rendering_usable) {
+		Log::WriteToConsoleAndLog("Conditional rendering is not used on this GPU.\n");
+	}
+	graphics.conditional_rendering_enabled =
+	    conditional_rendering.conditionalRendering && conditional_rendering_usable;
 	LOGF("Vulkan maintenance8 support: %s\n",
 	     graphics.maintenance8_enabled ? "true" : "false");
 	LOGF("Vulkan depth feedback support: %s\n",
